  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Arjunglucoside I and VMRC-LCP through a series of target interactions. Arjunglucoside I is implicated in targeting Hepatocyte, which in turn is a target of Myxotyroside B and Gramideoxybenzoin H, both of which ultimately target VMRC-LCP. Similarly, Arjunglucoside I is also linked to FaDu, which is a target of Calenduloside C, which also targets VMRC-LCP. These findings collectively indicate that Arjunglucoside I may act through multiple pathways to influence VMRC-LCP, likely by modulating the activity of downstream targets. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Arjunglucoside I affects VMRC-LCP remains to be elucidated. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction between Arjunglucoside I and VMRC-LCP.",
